from pathlib import Path
import json,pandas as pd,torch
P=Path(__file__).resolve().parents[1];R=P/'results';s=json.loads((R/'metrics/summary.json').read_text());e=pd.read_csv(R/'metrics/experiments.csv');h=pd.read_csv(R/'models/history.csv');q=json.loads((R/'metrics/quality.json').read_text());ck=torch.load(R/'models/stellar_cnn.pt',map_location='cpu',weights_only=True)
lines=['# Scientific technical report','', '## Scope and provenance','', 'This package implements and executes a new synthetic investigation. The original local project artifacts were not provided. Historical aggregate numbers are explicitly unverified. No real observations were used.','', '## Protocol','', '10,000 32 × 32 cutouts: 7,000 train, 1,000 validation, 2,000 test. Independent split seeds 20261016–18. Flux is log-uniform 100–3000 electrons; sigma is uniform 1.1–1.5 pixels; baseline sky is 20 electrons/pixel and read noise 3 electrons RMS. Unit-sum finite-stamp PSFs use 2 × 2 subpixel quadrature.','', 'Aperture: measured centroid, radius four, sky annulus 9–13, nominal sigma=1.3 correction. PSF: bounded single circular Gaussian fit, free flux/centre/width/background, seven-pixel fitting region. Ridge and residual Ridge: standardised image-derived features, alpha chosen by validation MAE. CNN: two convolutions, 8/16 channels, pooling, dense 32, scaled inputs/targets, Adam and validation selection.','',f'CNN trained for {len(h)} epochs. Best checkpoint: epoch {ck["epoch"]}. Test PSF optimisation failures: {q["fit_failure_count"]}/{q["test_count"]}.', '', '## Held-out results','', '|Method|MAE (e−)|RMSE (e−)|Bias (e−)|Median relative error (%)|95% MAE interval|','|---|---:|---:|---:|---:|---|']
for name,v in s.items():lines.append(f"|{name}|{v['mae']:.3f}|{v['rmse']:.3f}|{v['bias']:+.3f}|{v['median_relative_percent']:.3f}|{v['mae_95_bootstrap'][0]:.3f}–{v['mae_95_bootstrap'][1]:.3f}|")
lines+=['','## Paired comparisons','', 'Intervals are percentile bootstrap estimates from 1,000 resamples. Negative MAE differences favour the model over PSF. They condition on the trained model and exclude seed-to-seed training uncertainty.','']
for name,v in s.items():lines.append(f"- {name}: MAE difference {v['mae']-s['PSF']['mae']:+.3f} e−; 95% interval {v['mae_minus_psf_95_paired'][0]:+.3f} to {v['mae_minus_psf_95_paired'][1]:+.3f} e−.")
lines+=['','## Controlled conditions','', 'Each condition contains 200 observations, with identical images for every estimator. Parameters and raw arrays are saved. The common condition seed couples nuisance draws; changing Poisson means can change subsequent random draws. There are no scenario confidence intervals or corrected significance tests.','', '|Condition|Method|MAE (e−)|Bias (e−)|','|---|---|---:|---:|']
for _,r in e.iterrows():lines.append(f"|{r.experiment}|{r['method']}|{r.mae:.3f}|{r.bias:+.3f}|")
lines+=['','## Interpretation','',f"Ridge has MAE {s['Ridge']['mae']:.2f} electrons, residual Ridge {s['Residual']['mae']:.2f}, CNN {s['CNN']['mae']:.2f}, aperture {s['Aperture']['mae']:.2f}, and PSF {s['PSF']['mae']:.2f}. This run does not reproduce the historical PSF-first ranking. Neither comparison invalidates the other without matching data and estimator assumptions.", '',f"Grouped ablation changes Ridge MAE from {s['Ridge']['mae']:.2f} to {s['Ablation']['mae']:.2f}. This supports the usefulness of the removed group within this fit, not a causal claim for a particular feature. Residual and direct Ridge are closely related linear models because the baseline PSF estimate is itself a feature.", '', 'The free PSF width and centroid can absorb noise, especially on faint sources. A fixed aperture and learned prior may trade variance against bias. These are plausible mechanisms, not isolated causal conclusions. Test conditions outside the training distribution reveal sensitivity; rankings on 200 examples should not be overgeneralised.', '', '## Historical comparison', '', 'Historical user-reported MAE: aperture 61.13, PSF 54.63, Ridge 85.90, CNN 76.059 electrons. Historical split membership, metric definitions, weights and predictions could not be checked. Full historical values are preserved separately.', '', '## Reproduction and limitations', '', 'See README.md for stage commands, REPRODUCIBILITY.md for seeds and units, and SCIENTIFIC_LIMITATIONS.md for simulator and estimator caveats. All scientific plots come from saved outputs. No original data, real observations, multiple training seeds or M4 hardware validation were available. Browser rendering and Vercel-host deployment were not tested.', '', '## Sources', '', '- Photutils aperture documentation: https://photutils.readthedocs.io/en/stable/user_guide/aperture.html', '- Kingma & Ba, Adam: https://arxiv.org/abs/1412.6980', '- scikit-learn Ridge: https://scikit-learn.org/stable/modules/generated/sklearn.linear_model.Ridge.html', '- Original Distill framework: https://github.com/distillpub/template', '- Design reference: https://distill.pub/2021/gnn-intro/']
(P/'report/TECHNICAL_REPORT.md').write_text('\n'.join(lines)+'\n')
print('Technical report written')
